Appointment of Michael Godown to the Tourism Promotion Joint Powers Board, and Tim
Thorson to the City-County Health Board.  Ms. Broyles moved to approve, seconded by Mr.
Brown.  Ms. Broyles moved to divide the question to allow for a separate vote on the
appointment of Tim Thorson, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body present with the exception of Mayor Kaysen who did not vote
(Mayoral appointment). Ms. Broyles moved to postpone action on the appointment of Mr.
Thorson for 2 weeks (to Nov. 8, 2010), seconded by Mr. Collins.  Mayor Kaysen advised Mr.
Thorson had requested the postponement.  Motion to postpone carried.  Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body present with the exception of Mayor Kaysen who did not vote
(Mayoral appointment).  Main motion to approve the appointment of Michael Godown carried.
Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present with the exception of Mayor Kaysen
who did not vote (Mayoral appointment).
Appointment of Kadi Davis, Ian Dome, Jay Egan-Wright, Karolyn Hopfensperger, Dean
Jackson, John Matsen, Bobby McGarry, Monica Mencer,  McKinzea Olsen, Jacob Peterson Gary
Sayler, Isaiah Sims, Josh Walker, and  Sabrina Westover to the Mayor’s Youth Council. Mr.
Collins moved to approve, seconded by Ms. Ash.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members
of the governing body present with the exception of Mayor Kaysen who did not vote (Mayoral
appointments).
Announcement was made of the appointment of Greggory Crisp to the Mayor’s Council
for People with Disabilities, Frank Harris to the  Tourism Promotion Joint Powers Board d/b/a
Visit Cheyenne, Ross McKelvey to the Laramie County Community Juvenile Services Joint
Powers Board, and Mel Wilkenfield to the Water Conservation Advisory Committee to be
confirmed November 8, 2010. Mayor Kaysen announced an administrative correction to the
agenda item relative to the proposed appointment of Mr. Wilkenfield, stating the appointment
was being withdrawn from the agenda as approval is not required by the governing body.  He
explained Water Conservation Advisory Committee members are appointed pursuant to
recommendation from the Board of Public Utilities with approval by the Mayor.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, Mayor Kaysen
adjourned the meeting at 7:47 p.m.
